      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "General solvothermal procedure for {Ni8Ln8}: H4TC4A (0.05 mmol), Ni(OAc)2·4H2O (0.2 mmol), Ln(NO3)3·6H2O (0.1 mmol; Ln = Gd for this compound), 2,2-bis(hydroxymethyl)propionic acid (0.1 mmol) and triethanolamine (0.1 mmol) were dissolved in DMF/MeOH/MeCN/H2O. The solution was stirred for 2 h at room temperature, sealed in a 20 mL Teflon-lined autoclave and heated at 160 °C for 3 days, then cooled to room temperature. Pale blue blocky crystals formed (yield 75% based on Ln(NO3)3·6H2O). Solvent ratio for {Ni8Gd8}: DMF/MeOH/MeCN/H2O = 1 mL/4 mL/4 mL/0.5 mL. Crystals were dried in vacuum at room temperature for 48 h before elemental analysis.",
